  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Kout Bo 6. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Kout Bo 6 (or simply Koutbo6) is a high-stakes, team-based trick-taking game popular in Egypt, Kuwait, and across the Arab world. Played by two teams of three (6 players total), it utilizes 54 cards (standard 52 + 2 Jokers). It is a game of bidding, where the winning team's contract (Hokm) dictates the trump suit, and the Red and Black Jokers serve as the most powerful permanent trumps.",
    objective: 'As the bidding team, fulfill your contract (win the number of tricks bid). As the defenders, prevent them from doing so.',
    gameplay: '1. Must follow suit. If unable, play any card.\n2. Jokers can be played even if a player HAS the suit led.\n3. Leading a Joker forces all other players to play a Trump card if they have one.',
    keyRules: [
      'Must follow suit when able; if void may play any card including trump or Joker.',
      'Jokers may be played to an existing trick anytime; leading a Joker has restrictions (bid 8/9 or trump face cards played).',
      'High bidder declares trump (Hokm); Red and Black Jokers are permanent trumps, Color Joker highest.',
      'Bid 5 (Bab) to 9 (Bawan); if first five pass, dealer must bid at least 5 (Malzom).',
      'First to 101 points wins; or 51+ vs 0; or Bawan made on first hand.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
